{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Desirable</b> — The people of the world desire to have much gold and fine gold; they are precious stones because they endure and one finds them at the time of need, because they stand by themselves and do not fail. But wisdom has advantage over them, for a man finds it both in his life and in his death." "<b>And the meaning of \"and sweet\"</b> — For food is needed by every living thing, good and bad. He said: For the delight of wisdom is greater than the delight of sweet food, and nothing is above honey, because food is a fleeting pleasure while wisdom is forever." "<b>Also the meaning of \"sweet, more than honey and honeycomb\"</b> — to the discerning alone, not to every man; therefore also \"your servant.\" And the word בהם (in them) is like הנחמדים (desirable). And the meaning of \"in keeping them is great reward\": I know that in their keeping, great reward the keeper receives, and behold they benefit in this world and in the world to come."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "ובבא (\"and in the world to come\") is an unusual spelling for ובבא, likely an abbreviation or variant for ובבא (ועולם הבא); translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:56.273537411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}